TSN regression ITF options

# Specify type of config built by Makefile
--makefile_cfgs=config-3 or --makefile_cfgs=tsn-concurrent or --makefile_cfgs=config-3,tsn-concurrent
 
# Specify fixed or random seed
--fixed_seed=1 or --fixed_seed=0

# Specify number of seeds
ex. --num_seeds=20

# Specify seed
ex. --seed=7

# Enable coverage
--cov_en=1

# Specify farm or local run
--farm or --localr

# Specify regression list to be used
ex. --regr_list=regression_list.txt
* see below for how to structure the regression_list.txt to allow for different options for each test

# Specify testname
ex. --testname=eth_gdr_base_test

# Specify sequence
ex. --sequence=tsn_mphy_rst_seq

# Enable BANDWIDTH_ON compile +arg for perf tests
--perf_en=1

# Enable xprop
--xprop=1

# Enable dump
--dump_on=1

# Enable fsdb dump
--fdsb_on=1

# Specify max number of errors
--error_count=20000

##############################################
## How to format regression_list.txt ##
##############################################

Follow this format
testname=<your testname> --sequence=<your sequence> [other options like num_seed or fixed_seed here]
ex.
testname=eth_gdr_base_test --sequence=tsn_sanity_sequence --fixed_seed=0 --num_seeds=20
testname=eth_gdr_base_test --sequence=tsn_

##############################################
How to view coverage
##############################################

1. run the ./get_cov.sh script
2. dve -cov -full64 -dir gbx_cov_merged.vdb -elfile <your_exclusion_file.el>

## Examples ##

Run the 'eth_gdr_base_test' with sequence 'tsn_mphy_rst_seq' for seed='7' locally and output log to a file called 'run.txt'  
reg_exe --localr --testname=eth_gdr_base_test --sequence=tsn_mphy_rst_seq --seed=7 2>&1 | tee run.txt

Start a regression on the farm using 'regression_list.txt'
reg_exe --farm --priority=50 --regr_list=regression_list.txt

Start a regression on the farm with coverage enabled
reg_exe --farm --priority=50 --regr_list=regression_list.txt --cov_en=1 --return-file-mode=all --job-clean-mode=no_clean






